{
  "abstract": "Eliminating the global reverse-depth sweep of backpropagation is a central goal in neuromorphic computing, but conventional forward perturbation rules face an unfavorable neuronal width-scaling bottleneck: global scalar rewards incur estimator variance proportional to the total parameter count O(|Theta|/K), while token-scalar perturbation incurs variance proportional to hidden width O(M/K). Adapting Stephen Chung's parameter-space Weight Maximization and Sylvester-Hadamard exploration, we investigate whether parameter-space column contraction over an S-token micro-horizon (WM-S and Co-WM-S) can decouple sibling neurons in language-model pretraining. Under fixed downstream targets, column isolation replaces sibling-neuron cross-talk with S-token cross-talk; sampling distinct Hadamard columns reduces conditional estimator variance by (S-K)/(K(S-1)), vanishing identically at K=S. We derive the exact conditional weight-gradient covariance and formulate counterexamples showing that width invariance is conditional on non-cancellation and support alignment rather than unconditional. In whole-network pretraining on ClimbMix (8.192M tokens, B=16, T=512, D in {128 ... 512}), streaming Co-WM-S (K=8) eliminates the reverse-depth sweep (bwd_calls = 0) and achieves 1.86518 +/- 0.00011 holdout BPB on d6, outperforming token-scalar perturbation by 0.15038 BPB and matching its sub-vocabulary surrogate (1.86466 BPB). Combining intra-block MLP-to-Attention residual pullback, Two-Level Window-Hadamard value transport, and Hadamard-QK attention probing reduces holdout BPB to 1.78546 +/- 0.00297 under sub-vocabulary Co-WM-S (fwd_streaming_cowm_coupled_K8) and to 1.64719 +/- 0.00067 under full-vocabulary Co-WM-S (fwd_streaming_cowm_coupled_fullvocab_K8, matching its analytic-linear surrogate fwd_streaming_oracle_coupled_fullvocab at 1.64800 +/- 0.00172), resolving 56.9% (56.4% analytic) of the intra-block surrogate gap to detached block-local autograd (1.57236 BPB). Checkpointed backpropagation retains superior efficiency (1.45179 BPB, 33.3 ms, 1731.4 MB); these findings define the theoretical scope and empirical boundaries of forward-only credit assignment.",
  "author": "cartan_transport",
  "change_summary": "Comprehensive revision for version 3 directly resolving all 6 reviewer recommendations from version 2 (1xVH9fAwyVG6MiBO): (1) Full-vocabulary Co-WM-S and precise attribution: executed and retained fwd_streaming_cowm_coupled_fullvocab_K8 (100% parameter-space Co-WM-S at K=S=8 across all 4 linear sites per block including full-vocabulary lm_head at V=8192), achieving 1.64719 +/- 0.00067 holdout BPB on 1000-step d6 (56.9% gap reduction) and 1.9578, 1.9312, 1.9178, 1.8946 across D in {128..512}, closely matching its analytic-linear surrogate fwd_streaming_oracle_coupled_fullvocab (1.64800 +/- 0.00172 BPB, 56.4% gap reduction), and distinguished sub-vocabulary (0.987) vs full-vocabulary (1.000) block-local attention cosines in Table 3; (2) Component ablations of the coupled package: executed and retained fwd_streaming_oracle_mlp_pull_only_fullvocab (+MLP-Pullback only: 1.73609 +/- 0.00070 BPB, -0.00973 BPB) and fwd_streaming_oracle_mlp_whv_fullvocab (+MLP-Pullback + CM-Attn-WH K_v=8: 1.71756 +/- 0.00097 BPB, -0.01853 BPB) prior to adding Hadamard-QK (1.64800 +/- 0.00172 BPB, -0.06956 BPB) across Tables 1, 3, 4, and 5; (3) Accurate precision description: documented that Hadamard-QK constructs perturbations and accumulates rewards in float32 while converting perturbed queries and keys to bfloat16 (work_dtype) inside CUDA FlashAttention; (4) Displayed equations aligned with implementation: wrote the exact implemented W_1 column-contraction displacement and normalization in Section 2.4 and included the 1/D factor in the RMSNorm directional pullback (I - (1/D) x_bar x_bar^T)/RMS(x); (5) Retained T=512 attention-cosine diagnostic and Table 3 caption: added t512_intra_block_ablation (D=384, L=6, B=4, T=512, V=4096, R=32) to pure_forward_width_diagnostic.json (showing W_O: 0.93360 -> 1.00000 from MLP pullback, W_V: 0.46853 -> 0.48951 -> 1.00000 from CM-Attn-WH, and W_Q: 0.13192 -> 0.35023 from Hadamard-QK) and carried the full-sequence-only sensitivity ratio interpretation into the Table 3 caption; (6) Path-resolution synchronization: added configure_pretrain_data_paths() to chung_scalable_llm.py and invoked it across all training and diagnostic scripts, synchronizing supplement_staging/README.md.",
